3	// Real PersonaPlex full-duplex voice engine over a DIRECT browser→fal.ai
4	// WebSocket (no fal SDK — same direct-socket pattern as useXaiSession).
5	//
6	// Architecture: mint a short-lived JWT at /api/fal/token, then open
7	// `wss://fal.run/fal-ai/personaplex/realtime?fal_jwt_token=REDACTED Transport is
8	// MSGPACK binary frames both ways (verified by probe — the server silently
9	// ignores JSON text frames): we send `{audio: <raw PCM16 bytes>, …config}`
10	// continuously; the server streams back `{audio: <raw PCM16 bytes>, text}`.
11	//
12	// Full-duplex consequences (PersonaPlex is a Moshi-style model that listens
13	// while it speaks — see docs/personaplex-local-inference.md):
14	//   - The model speaks FIRST (trained to open the call) — no greeting bootstrap.
15	//   - There is no server VAD and no turn events: `interrupt()` is a no-op
16	//     (barge-in is native — just talk), and callState is derived from output
17	//     audio activity.
18	//   - No user-side transcript (no ASR anywhere in the path); the agent
19	//     transcript streams as inner-monologue text tokens.
20	//   - The mic is GATED to silence during the opening greeting (GreetingGate),
21	//     and autoGainControl is off, so room noise can't make the model interrupt
22	//     its own greeting. Muting likewise sends zeros — the input timeline must
23	//     stay continuous.
24	//   - Audio is fixed 24kHz PCM16 both ways: the AudioContext is constructed at
25	//     24kHz and the browser resamples mic/speaker at the edges.
26	//
27	// Exposes the same surface as useXaiSession so useRealtimeSession dispatches
28	// uniformly. Must be called unconditionally (rules of hooks); inert until start().
